commit 983e2c071d46f3deea68b911bb5e1f728783ba60

C03: the visible-click surface is captured on the named root window before and after the click (UI1397)

UI1395 measured «abrí la calculadora y apretá el 5» after the App admitted the click confirmation behind a verified app.open: the root approved every click on the launched Calculator, yet each ended failed as visible_button_postread_unchanged. A root probe with the provider's own launch (calc.exe, then RequestForeground on Process.MainWindowHandle) and DesktopClickVisible.ps1 showed why: before the click the foreground is the Calculator's CoreWindow (calculatorapp.exe, which owns no top-level window), and after the UIA invoke it is the ApplicationFrameHost frame. WindowsVisibleControlAdapter compares the before/after captures only when both bind the same hwnd, and the captures followed the foreground, so the surface comparison never ran.

VisibleControlSurface.CaptureForegroundAsync: the foreground window is normalized to its root ancestor (GetAncestor GA_ROOT), the frame that fronts both moments; a classic top-level window keeps the largest-window rule. The capture names that window instead of reading the active window again.
IScreenshotPlatform / GdiScreenshotPlatform / WindowsScreenshotProvider: CaptureWindow(nint) captures the named window's DWM bounds (clipped to the desktop, physical pixels) with the same provenance as the active-window capture; the interface member has a default so other platforms keep compiling.

Providers.Windows recompiled (BUILD1397). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


